The function $f(x) = \dfrac{x^{3}}{64}$ on $[0,b]$, and $0$ elsewhere, is a probability density function. Find $b$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.94cm, y=1.4cm]
\fill[gray!35, domain=0:4.6, variable=\x] (0,0) -- plot ({\x},{\x*\x*\x/64}) -- (4.6,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.5,0) -- (5.9,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,2.4) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.4,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick, domain=0:4.6, smooth, samples=100, variable=\x] plot ({\x},{\x*\x*\x/64});
\draw (4.6,0) -- (4.6,1.521);
\draw[thick] (4.6,0) -- (5.7,0);
\node[below] at (4.6,0) {$b$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The function $f(x) = \dfrac{1}{8}(5 - x)$ on $[0,c]$, and $0$ elsewhere, is a probability density function. Find $c$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.9cm, y=4cm]
\fill[gray!35] (0,0) -- (0,0.625) -- (3.2,0.225) -- (3.2,0) -- cycle;
\draw[->] (-0.6,0) -- (6.6,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.1) -- (0,0.9) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.5,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick] (0,0.625) -- (5,0);
\draw[thick] (5,0) -- (6.4,0);
\draw (3.2,0) -- (3.2,0.225);
\node[below] at (3.2,0) {$c$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A probability density function is $f(x) = k$ for $0 \le x < 4$ and $f(x) = 4k$ for $4 \le x \le 6$, and $0$ elsewhere. Find $k$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, x=0.78cm, y=1.0cm]
\draw[->] (-0.7,0) -- (7.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.3) node[above] {$f(x)$};
\draw[thick] (-0.6,0) -- (0,0);
\draw[thick] (0,0.6) -- (4,0.6);
\draw[thick] (4,2.4) -- (6,2.4);
\draw[dashed] (0,0.6) -- (0,0);
\draw[dashed] (4,0.6) -- (4,2.4);
\draw[dashed] (6,2.4) -- (6,0);
\draw[thick] (6,0) -- (7.2,0);
\node[left] at (0,0.6) {$k$};
\node[left] at (0,2.4) {$4k$};
\node[below] at (4,0) {$4$};
\node[below] at (6,0) {$6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
